  "notes": [
    "Every final admission attempt uses explicit 100,000 count settings; only 20,000 and 50,000 complete. Directories and administration push 100,000 source files above 100,000 inventory entries; staged Git metadata also exceeds the unchanged output bound.",
    "Parent and subprocess lifetime RSS peaks are separate; do not add them into an asserted combined peak.",
    "A completed record verifies an outside edit was installed in the private file, all requested safe points settled, and clean close retired the private root.",
    "Actual-default cleanup fixtures use 49,999 five-byte ordinary sources plus one .gitignore, exact .env consent and a non-signature private canary. Default Settings() supply counts. Both private seeds retire after manager restart; unknown ordinary build output is preserved in the second case.",
    "Actual-default open timing includes repository registration and session acknowledgement; the admission benchmark timing measures session.open after repository registration.",
    "These are small-file synthetic local receipts, not universal latency promises for arbitrary checkout contents or unsupported filesystems."
